<title>JAPAN: OSE says 20 firms eligible to list stock options.</title>
<headline>OSE says 20 firms eligible to list stock options.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Osaka Securities Exchange (OSE) on Monday announced that Sony Corp, Toyota Motor Corp, Nintendo Co Ltd and 17 other firms would be eligible to list stock options as of July 18.  </p>
<p>The Osaka bourse said it selected the shares based on the volume of the firms' listed stocks, recent turnover on the bourse and the liquidity of the shares. It said the decision was also made based on how international the firms are.</p>
<p>The following is a list of the companies which the OSE said would be eligible for individual stock options:</p>
<p>Toray Industries Inc</p>
<p>Takeda Chemical Industries Ltd</p>
<p>Bridgestone Corp</p>
<p>Nippon Steel Corp</p>
<p>Hitachi Ltd</p>
<p>NEC Corp</p>
<p>Matsushita Electric Industrial Co</p>
<p>Sony Corp</p>
<p>Rohm Co Ltd</p>
<p>Kyocera Corp</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd</p>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp</p>
<p>Honda Motor Co Ltd</p>
<p>Nintendo Co</p>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp</p>
<p>Mitsui &amp; Co</p>
<p>Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd</p>
<p>Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd</p>
<p>Sumitomo Bank Ltd</p>
<p>Tokio Marine &amp; Fire Insurance Co</p>
</text>
